{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_019TvT4vFtnqQNpfCkqfcRxg","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"PostgreSQL latest release minor version October 2026\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"PostgreSQL: Release Notes\",\"url\":\"https://www.postgresql.org/docs/release/\"},{\"title\":\"PostgreSQL: PostgreSQL 18.6, 17.11, 16.15, 15.19, 14.24 and 19 Beta 3 Released!\",\"url\":\"https://www.postgresql.org/about/news/postgresql-186-1711-1615-1519-1424-and-19-beta-3-released-3365/\"},{\"title\":\"PostgreSQL: Versioning Policy\",\"url\":\"https://www.postgresql.org/support/versioning/\"},{\"title\":\"PostgreSQL: The world's most advanced open source database\",\"url\":\"https://www.postgresql.org/\"},{\"title\":\"PostgreSQL: PostgreSQL 18.4, 17.10, 16.14, 15.18, and 14.23 Released!\",\"url\":\"https://www.postgresql.org/about/news/postgresql-184-1710-1614-1518-and-1423-released-3297/\"},{\"title\":\"PostgreSQL: PostgreSQL 19 Beta 4 Released!\",\"url\":\"https://www.postgresql.org/about/news/postgresql-19-beta-4-released-3386/\"},{\"title\":\"PostgreSQL: PostgreSQL 18.3, 17.9, 16.13, 15.17, and 14.22 Released!\",\"url\":\"https://www.postgresql.org/about/news/postgresql-183-179-1613-1517-and-1422-released-3246/\"},{\"title\":\"PostgreSQL: PostgreSQL 19 RC 1 Released!\",\"url\":\"https://www.postgresql.org/about/news/postgresql-19-rc-1-released-3409/\"},{\"title\":\"PostgreSQL: PostgreSQL 18.2, 17.8, 16.12, 15.16, and 14.21 Released!\",\"url\":\"https://www.postgresql.org/about/news/postgresql-182-178-1612-1516-and-1421-released-3235/\"},{\"title\":\"PostgreSQL: PostgreSQL 18 Released!\",\"url\":\"https://www.postgresql.org/about/news/postgresql-18-released-3142/\"}]\n\nThe newest PostgreSQL minor releases are 18.6, 17.11, 16.15, 15.19, and 14.24, which came out about 65 days ago (roughly August 2026), so there has been no minor release in October. The 18.6 release also skipped 18.5, which was pulled because of a regression. The next scheduled minor update is November 12, 2026, and the project says it will be large. The PostgreSQL Global Development Group has released an update to all supported versions of PostgreSQL, including 18.6, 17.11, 16.15, 15.19, and 14.24. This release skips PostgreSQL 18 versions from PostgreSQL 18.4 to 18.6. 18.5 was not shipped due to a regression.\n\nThe major news this month is PostgreSQL 19. Its first release candidate came out on October 15, 2026. The release team plans to issue a second release candidate, PostgreSQL 19 RC 2, on November 12, 2026. Unless an issue is discovered that requires a delay or an additional release candidate, PostgreSQL 19 should be made generally available on November 19, 2026.\n\nA related date: PostgreSQL 14 will stop receiving fixes on November 12, 2026.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"82351f09-7e56-4b74-a9e0-f7a4bc9d57d4","uuid":"04fd23b9-dded-4f7d-98ad-e532951e80e9","timestamp":"2026-10-17T02:40:05.096Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"PostgreSQL latest release minor version October 2026","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_014ZznfqBKNhbL5RZAedgKZz","content":[{"title":"PostgreSQL: Release Notes","url":"https://www.postgresql.org/docs/release/"},{"title":"PostgreSQL: PostgreSQL 18.6, 17.11, 16.15, 15.19, 14.24 and 19 Beta 3 Released!","url":"https://www.postgresql.org/about/news/postgresql-186-1711-1615-1519-1424-and-19-beta-3-released-3365/"},{"title":"PostgreSQL: Versioning Policy","url":"https://www.postgresql.org/support/versioning/"},{"title":"PostgreSQL: The world's most advanced open source database","url":"https://www.postgresql.org/"},{"title":"PostgreSQL: PostgreSQL 18.4, 17.10, 16.14, 15.18, and 14.23 Released!","url":"https://www.postgresql.org/about/news/postgresql-184-1710-1614-1518-and-1423-released-3297/"},{"title":"PostgreSQL: PostgreSQL 19 Beta 4 Released!","url":"https://www.postgresql.org/about/news/postgresql-19-beta-4-released-3386/"},{"title":"PostgreSQL: PostgreSQL 18.3, 17.9, 16.13, 15.17, and 14.22 Released!","url":"https://www.postgresql.org/about/news/postgresql-183-179-1613-1517-and-1422-released-3246/"},{"title":"PostgreSQL: PostgreSQL 19 RC 1 Released!","url":"https://www.postgresql.org/about/news/postgresql-19-rc-1-released-3409/"},{"title":"PostgreSQL: PostgreSQL 18.2, 17.8, 16.12, 15.16, and 14.21 Released!","url":"https://www.postgresql.org/about/news/postgresql-182-178-1612-1516-and-1421-released-3235/"},{"title":"PostgreSQL: PostgreSQL 18 Released!","url":"https://www.postgresql.org/about/news/postgresql-18-released-3142/"}]},"The newest PostgreSQL minor releases are 18.6, 17.11, 16.15, 15.19, and 14.24, which came out about 65 days ago (roughly August 2026), so there has been no minor release in October. The 18.6 release also skipped 18.5, which was pulled because of a regression. The next scheduled minor update is November 12, 2026, and the project says it will be large. The PostgreSQL Global Development Group has released an update to all supported versions of PostgreSQL, including 18.6, 17.11, 16.15, 15.19, and 14.24. This release skips PostgreSQL 18 versions from PostgreSQL 18.4 to 18.6. 18.5 was not shipped due to a regression.\n\nThe major news this month is PostgreSQL 19. Its first release candidate came out on October 15, 2026. The release team plans to issue a second release candidate, PostgreSQL 19 RC 2, on November 12, 2026. Unless an issue is discovered that requires a delay or an additional release candidate, PostgreSQL 19 should be made generally available on November 19, 2026.\n\nA related date: PostgreSQL 14 will stop receiving fixes on November 12, 2026."],"durationSeconds":5.933743237999999,"searchCount":1},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_019TvT4vFtnqQNpfCkqfcRxg","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
